## 11. Failure analysis

Corrected wording: of the 45 held-out ATTRIBUTE scenarios V2 answered 34 (20 correct, **14 wrong**) and abstained on 11. **All 14 wrong answers named a service downstream
of the true root and all were SEMI_DIRECTED** (the earlier description "14 of 20 incorrect" was imprecise).

{{TABLE:tax_wrong}}

Unsafe on ABSTAIN_REQUIRED (held-out): 23 of 63 (WEAK_SIGNAL 12, SYMMETRIC_MUTUAL_DEPENDENCY 6, ROOT_UNOBSERVED 3, NO_DISCRIMINATING_EVIDENCE 2); in 10 of them the named service is a true root
but the evidence cannot support the claim. dev/val mechanism analysis (unchanged V2, no held-out re-run): the true root fails R3 because FCI leaves it isolated (dev 8, val 5 of 14 / 13 wrong answers),
so a later downstream node passes R3 and R4. Details by category (11 categories, each with definition, count, ids, root cause, class, remediation and risk) are in
`docs/SPRINT4_3_0_FAILURE_TAXONOMY.md`. No remedy that merely forces a root-cause answer is proposed.

